{
  "category": "records_per_sample",
  "version": "2.0",
  "description": "Cross-binding conformance for record axes (esm-spec \u00a78.5.1): a data-fed parameter receives two records per query time exactly when its record shape (its declared `shape`, or a shapeless parameter's `param_to_var` targets' declared shapes) begins with an `interval` index set carrying `\"records\": true`, and one otherwise; and for the deprecated `from.records_per_sample` / `temporal.records_per_sample` (\u00a78.3), which are still accepted with a load-time warning but must agree with the shape. Each `valid` case must load, validate with none of `record_codes`, and flatten; each listed `loader_fields` entry must report the number of records the parameter receives in `records_per_sample`; `flattened_from_records_per_sample` pins that the flattened parameter's `update.from` keeps the deprecated field exactly as written (`null` = absent); the index sets' `records` flag and the field survive emit then load; and the binding's deprecated-site function must return exactly `deprecated_fields` (JSON pointers, sorted), the places the load-time `deprecated_records_per_sample` warning names (the warning is emitted once per load when the list is non-empty, and not at all when it is empty). Each `invalid` case is schema-valid and must be refused by structural validation with exactly one diagnostic whose code is in `record_codes`: `code` at `pointer`. Each `flatten_invalid` case must validate with none of `record_codes` and then be refused by `flatten` with `code`, the message or details naming `pointer`. Each `refused` case must be refused with `code` by validation or by flatten, whichever first sees the record shape. Files under `fixtures/components/` are mounted or imported by the cases and are not cases themselves. `metadata.esio_format` is carried on every source and changes nothing.",
  "record_codes": [
    "record_axis_invalid",
    "record_axis_misplaced",
    "record_axis_time_invariant_source",
    "records_per_sample_invalid"
  ],
  "deprecation_warning": "deprecated_records_per_sample",
  "bindings": [
    "julia",
    "python",
    "rust",
    "typescript",
    "go"
  ],
